DiskSweep beta kit (10 testers)

RECRUIT: 1 Ableton/plugin user, 1 Xcode user, 1 Docker user, 1 Ollama/HF user,
1 photographer (large media), 5 general Mac users. macOS 14+.

GIVE EACH TESTER:
1. The DMG + its .sha256 (verify before opening).
2. This instruction: run DiskSweep, press Dry Run, screenshot the table,
   do NOT press Move to Trash on REVIEW rows on first run.

ASK FOR (paste into reply):
- macOS version / chip (arm64 or Intel):
- Dry-run SAFE total / REVIEW total:
- False SAFE (should have been REVIEW/BLOCKED — path + why):
- False REVIEW (obviously safe — path + why):
- Missing (big folder you expected listed but wasn't):
- Crash / hang / permission loop (what + where):
- Undo test: trash one SAFE cache dir, restore via Undo — worked?

EXIT CRITERIA: zero data-loss reports, zero BLOCKED bypasses, uninstall
(drag to Trash) leaves no daemon/helper (check /Library/LaunchDaemons for
com.nitedsp.* — must be absent).

Every valid false-SAFE/false-BLOCKED report becomes one new policy test
in tests/test_policy.py before the fix lands.
